  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "b8773f7cb0b53cb9e85671ad543af4af228d3c49",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 443095870,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "This is a pretty generic one.   tools/check_tfs.py already looks for places where dissectors redefine entries already in epan/tfs.c - I don't know if it'll show other dissectors that could use this new one?\n\ntools/check_tfs.py --common looks for entries that appear multiple times and might make sense to add to epan/tfs.c. It only reports ones that appear at least 3 times.  Current output is:\n\n('Optimised for signalling traffic', 'Not optimised for signalling traffic') appears 3 times, in:  ['epan/dissectors/packet-gsm_a_gm.c', 'epan/dissectors/packet-gsm_map.c', 'epan/dissectors/packet-gtp.c']\n\n('Data PDU', 'Control PDU') appears 3 times, in:  ['epan/dissectors/packet-pdcp-lte.c', 'epan/dissectors/packet-pdcp-nr.c', 'epan/dissectors/packet-rlc-nr.c']\n\n('Message sent to originating side', 'Message sent from originating side') appears 3 times, in:  ['epan/dissectors/packet-q2931.c', 'epan/dissectors/packet-q931.c', 'epan/dissectors/packet-q933.c']\n\n\nI resisted adding these to epan/tfs.c because they sound quite specialised, but thinking about it now maybe I will.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/030414c33f619ee28811cd9c073802ef2267d160ab2744eb8427bd49af4c7998?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/martin.r.mathieson"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-11-06T12:14:30.828Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-11-06T13:29:12.311Z",
          "system": false,
